Package, depgraph: an ebuild with unaccepted KEYWORDS is not visible; its other masks and its USE stay lazy

Sub-series: O (stage 4, round 2) - patch 1 of 3; needs 0001-0031 (the depgraph hunks touch code of 0031).
Base: upstream 73646c35d.

Package.visible asks _getMissingKeywords() first. An ebuild that is not
installed and has unaccepted KEYWORDS is not visible whatever its other masks
are (_eval_visibility), so the answer is given without the rest of
_eval_masks(): validating the dependency strings and computing the USE that
the conditionals in LICENSE, PROPERTIES and RESTRICT need. About a third of the
ebuilds a resolve looks at end this way. The masks property still computes the
complete dict by the unchanged _eval_masks() for whoever asks (autounmask,
messages). In depgraph.py the places that computed USE for such a package only
to pass it along now leave it alone.

Judge, four alternating passes, medians: 0001-0031 + 0033 + 0034 85.3 s -> with
this patch 83.4 s (about -2 s). Alone on 0001-0031 it is inside the noise
(87.9 against 87.2 s, three passes).
Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in stage 4 of the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-21, on
upstream commit 73646c35d with patches 0001-0030 and the C modules applied. Not a
human-written change. Judge: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of one system image, six
resolves in parallel, wall seconds summed; every run gave the same merge list in the same
order and the same number of backtracking attempts as unpatched 73646c35d. Black-box
testers (invented states, reference against candidate): 0 differences.

The author of patches 0032-0034 was killed by the kernel (memory limit) at its
last step and left NO report; the description above is from its code comments
and from a line-by-line review. Its lock-step outputs survive: 35 runs on about
20 states, 59,111 visibility and mask comparisons, 42,017 USE comparisons,
0 mismatches. Tester: 12 probes on 0031-0034 together.

